.SS "void crayon::ThreadPool::shutdown ()\fR [noexcept]\fP"

.PP
Requests this \fBThreadPool\fP to gracefully shutdown after draining and executing all the queued and inflight tasks, respectively, disallows future \fBtask submissions\fP, and returns immediately without waiting for this \fBThreadPool\fP to fully shutdown\&. To explicitly control whether to wait until complete shutdown, use \fBThreadPool::shutdown(bool)\fP\&.

.PP
This overload is thread-safe and may be called concurrently with task submission and with other non-blocking shutdown requests, provided that this object's lifetime remains active\&.

.PP
This is an idempotent, irreversible operation\&. Once shutdown is successfully requested, this \fBThreadPool\fP can no longer be used to process tasks\&. Unless you absolutely need to explicitly request shutdown before the end of the scope is reached, prefer letting the compiler shut this \fBThreadPool\fP down on destruction at the end of the scope\&. 
.PP
Definition at line \fB137\fP of file \fBthread_pool\&.cpp\fP\&.
.SS "void crayon::ThreadPool::shutdown (bool wait)\fR [noexcept]\fP"

.PP
Requests this \fBThreadPool\fP to gracefully shutdown after draining and executing all the queued and inflight tasks, respectively, disallows future \fBtask submissions\fP, and only waits for this \fBThreadPool\fP to fully shutdown if \fRwait\fP is explicitly requested\&. When \fRwait\fP is \fRfalse\fP, this operation is thread-safe and may be called concurrently with task submission and other non-blocking shutdown requests while this object's lifetime remains active\&.

.PP
When \fRwait\fP is \fRtrue\fP, the caller must ensure that no other blocking shutdown or destruction executes concurrently\&. It must also not be called from a worker thread owned by this same pool\&.

.PP
Waiting is cooperative\&. This function may block indefinitely if an executing task never returns or waits on work that cannot make progress\&.

.PP
This is an idempotent, irreversible operation\&. Once shutdown is successfully requested, this \fBThreadPool\fP can no longer be used to process tasks\&. Unless you absolutely need to explicitly request shutdown before the end of the scope is reached, prefer letting the compiler shut this \fBThreadPool\fP down on destruction at the end of the scope\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwait\fP Whether to wait until every worker has finished and been joined\&. 
.RE
.PP

